properties.description:
Cut 2026-10-26 on Anthony's word ("go on the release, starting with the stack check"; the stack check failed on 0.91.0's code, he chose explicit work stacks plus a 16 MiB runtime stack, #802 merged, then "Resume STAGE 2"), in PR release/v0.92.0. The tag push stays his. A minor carrying:
- #794: slash commands that front a skill are thin pointers; what they asked for moved into the skills;
- #795: open_breach (open defect findings, exceeded limits, VIOLATES into a limit, must-fix rule violations) in loop_status and detect_gaps; composition: each;
- #796: a premise reads as its owner's intent or its delivery; a step concluding a Decision reads intent by default (add_inference as_intent / as_delivery);
- #797: a null unsets a field at every typed constructor;
- #798: find_tools finds relations; what_joins;
- #799: record_the_build; add_change_event answers; loop_status fixes_answering_nothing and repairs; record_change and manual_work_report removed (deprecated in 0.91.0);
- #800: add_artifact inputs, owed_computations and resting_on_stale_numbers, propagate_from redo_list;
- #801: reasoning evaluated once per report, circle readings kept;
- #802: foundations_walk and proof_chain_walk on explicit work stacks; server runtime threads at 16 MiB.

199 tools (200 in 0.91.0: record_the_build added, two stubs removed); measured against the published 0.91.0 binary, twelve served tools differ. 34 skills, every body gains its "When it is run as /<command>" section; capture-intent and detect-and-ask also changed. get_instructions gains one paragraph. The schema stamp moves by vocabulary only (Constraint.composition gains each; 28 node and 69 edge types as before), so docs/upgrading-to-v0.92.0.md is written, measured with the published 0.91.0 binary: 0.91.0 opens a store 0.92.0 opened (behind warning) and refuses one holding composition each. Re-probed at the cut on the 0.92.0 release build over HTTP: get_node at depth 4,000 and 5,000 and loop_status / detect_gaps on holding chains of 2,000 and 3,000 all answered, none aborted. Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018ibUbMKCS1yK5W17cncp9P
